  "term": "stimulant withdrawal",
  "definition": "Stimulant withdrawal is the state that occurs after stopping or reducing repeated, extended use of stimulant drugs such as methamphetamine or amphetamine. In the supplied source, it is described as showing variable effects, with some evidence of increased, decreased, or unchanged spontaneous movement during withdrawal depending on factors such as the specific stimulant and study conditions.",
